Use Lifebloom on the tank to spend Omen of Clarity procs;"},{["spellID"]=48438,["name"]="Wild Growth",["icon"]="Interface\\Icons\\Ability_Druid_Flourish",["condition"]="Use Wild Growth when available on groups of damaged allies;"},{["spellID"]=9840,["name"]="Rejuvenation",["icon"]="Interface\\Icons\\Spell_Nature_Rejuvenation",["condition"]="Use Rejuvenation on anyone taking damage, preferably Rogues, Warriors, and Death Knights for maximum Revitalize DPS value."}}}},["pvp"]={["overview"]={["ruRU"]={"Подвижный лекарь с периодическим лечением и контролем.","Может сочетать поддержание лечения, контроль и восстановление маны.","Неверный выход на контроль оставляет союзника без поддержки."},["enUS"]={"Restoration Druids have a unique healing style that relies on instant heals over time which act slowly, but also carry more potential healing in them than most casted heals of other classes.","",""}},["rotation"]={["ruRU"]="Сначала обеспечьте союзнику лечение, затем ищите безопасный момент для контроля или питья. Поддерживайте периодические эффекты заранее; срочное лечение и позиционирование важнее фиксированной последовательности заклинаний.",["enUS"]="Rather than a fixed rotation, Druid gameplay is about treading a fine balance between healing, drinking, and crowd controlling. In a nutshell: Keep yourself alive with Dire Bear Form and Barkskin; Stay in control of the match with Entangling Roots and Cyclone; Heal through enemy damage with Lifebloom, Rejuvenation, Wild Growth, Regrowth, and also Nature's Swiftness in emergencies; Keep your Mana topped with Innervate and by tactically slipping away to drink when allies are safe."},["builds"]={{["key"]="pvp_0",["title"]="Restoration Druid Standard PvP Talent Build (13/0/58)",["talentsString"]="053200012--230033312031502331350313251",["targetLevel"]=80,["points"]=71,["allocations"]={{["talentID"]=2238,["rank"]=5,["spellID"]=57814,["tree"]=1,["minLevel"]=10,["maxRank"]=5,["name"]="Genesis",["nameRu"]="Genesis"},{["talentID"]=78